            <p>This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the GNU Affero General Public License for more details.</p>
            <h3>AGPL Remote Network Interaction Nuance</h3>
            <small class="general-infohelp">This does not constitute legal advice or interpretation. For questions, consult a lawyer.</small>
            <p>The GNU Affero General Public License (AGPL) grants you a right to access a program's source code if you interact with it over a network. The applicability of this to a predominantly static-generated site is unclear.</p>
            <p>For the public-facing pages, this is most apparent: pages are statically generated using configuration data (database entries and CMS data), and the output is delivered to users over the Internet. As such, since configuration data is not subject to the AGPL, and an AGPL program's output is not necessarily licensed under the AGPL, interacting with the public-facing website output of this program is unlikely to trigger the AGPL's automatic downstream licensing provision (though it may cover in-line and first-party scripts).</p>
            <p>However, this does not apply to the administrative services: since administrative services pages and its API interact with the program in real time when you access it over a computer network, you are likely subject to its automatic downstream licensing provision. Therefore, a link to receive the source code is provided above.</p>
